# Keep the diagnostic and credential tools out of release archives.
#
# GitHub builds the "Source code (zip)" and "(tar.gz)" assets on a
# release with git archive, which honours export-ignore. Nothing under
# tools/ belongs in one: several of these scripts write to a charger,
# and get_tokens.py handles a Daze username and password, which must
# never reach a Home Assistant host.
#
# What this does not do, so nobody is misled by it: export-ignore only
# affects archive exports. Every file below stays in the repository,
# stays visible on GitHub, and still arrives with a git clone. It is not
# a way to hide anything — it keeps the tools out of the artefact people
# install from, nothing more.
#
# HACS is already covered separately and does not depend on this:
# hacs.json sets no zip_release, so HACS installs custom_components/daze
# alone. tests/test_release_excludes_tools.py holds both halves in place.
tools/ export-ignore

# Named as well as covered by the directory rule above, because this is
# the one whose presence in a release would matter most.
tools/get_tokens.py export-ignore
